{title: Free Indeed}
{subtitle: John 8:36}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]We claim the blood of Abraham [F/A]runs deep
[Gm]We say we have never been [Eb]anyone's slave
[Bb]But you ask how we could ever be [F/A]truly free
When the [Gm]chains of sin are [Eb]heavy and strong
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Truly, truly, I tell [F]you today
[Gm]Everyone who commits sin [Eb]is a slave
A [Bb]slave does not remain [F]in the house
But a [Gm]son stays for[Eb]ever in his [Bb]place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If the Son sets you free [F/A]from the bond
[Gm]You will be free indeed, tru[Eb]ly free
[Bb]I know your lineage, I [F/A]know your name
But my [Gm]word finds no room [Eb]in your heart
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I [Eb]speak of what I have seen with my [Bb]Father
You [Eb]do what you have heard from your [Gm]father
[Eb]If you were children of Ab[Gm]raham then
You would do the [Eb]works that he did
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Free in[Bb]deed, the son re[F/A]mains
Free in[Gm]deed, the chains are [Eb]gone
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |
